  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 102 AM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nAs of 1 AM CDT, temperatures around the area are in the low to mid \n60s with winds out of the east at around 10 mph. Some showers have \nmoved into central SD. The chance of accumulations of more than \n0.10\" are 30 to 50% along and southwest of a line from Eagle Butte \nto Chamberlain. Cooler temperatures continue today with highs in the \n80s. HRRR Smoke continues to show some concentrations of smoke aloft \nand a little at the surface. Might have a slight smokey smell to the \nair and slightly hazy skies today but not much impact past that. \n\nCooler temperatures continue into Thursday. Shower with maybe a\nrumble of thunder or two return during the daylight hours \nThursday across south central SD. Models are showing the low \nprompting these storms farther south than previously forecast so\nthe precipitation chances have also moved south. Few chances \nfor precipitation exist past this. There is a 30-50% chance of \nmore than 0.10\" of rainfall south of Pierre. A warm front moves \nacross the area Friday bringing a return to above average \ntemperatures through the weekend. Actual temperatures are \nforecast to be higher than the last round of heat, at least over\ncentral SD, with highs in the mid 100s. Might need to lower \nhigh temperatures over eastern SD for the weekend due to a high \nbias with higher humidity values. The heat seems to lessen going\ninto next work week but stays above average.",
